{"text": "Centennial Care:\n\nEnsuring care for New Mexicans for the next 100 years and beyond\n\nInternal Timeline for Release\n\nFebruary 17, 2012 - Invite Legislators (LFC and LHHS Committee members) to\nattend meeting outlining the Centennial Care concept paper scheduled for February\n21, 2012 in Albuquerque.\nFebruary 17, 2012 - Issue letters to Tribal leaders inviting them to a Tribal\nConsultation for the Centennial Care Concept Paper. (Consultation being scheduled\nfor the week of March 19, 2012)\nFebruary 20, 2012 - Invite advocates and media to release of Medicaid\nModernization Concept paper\nFebruary 21, 2012 - Send letter and e-mail to Tribal leaders sharing a hard copy of\nthe Medicaid Modernization concept paper and the link to the concept paper on the\nHSD website.\nFebruary 21, 2012 - Internal email goes to management staff with a copy of the\npaper and the ok to release to other staff\nFebruary 21, 2012 - Conduct individual meetings to release the Medicaid\nModernization Concept Paper\no Meet with Barry Massey, AP - 7:30a.m to 8:30a.m.\nMeet with Journal Editorial Board - 10:00a.m. to 11:00a.m.\nMedia Briefing - 12:00p.m. to 1:00p.m.\nLegislators Briefing - 1:15p.m to 2:15p.m.\nStakeholders Briefing - 2:30p.m. to 3:30p.m.\no Issue News Release - 2:15p.m.\n\noo Oo Oo\n\nFebruary 22, 2012 - Bob Clark Radio Show and any follow-up media inquiries from\nmeetings/release the day before\nMarch 5, 2012 - Medicaid Advisory Committee (MAC) meeting. Morning meeting\n(closed) with members on the MAC to go over details of the concept paper. The\nafternoon regular MAC meeting will allow the opportunity for public comment.\nMarch 2012 - Behavioral Health Expert Panel meeting. Will go over the concept\npaper with the expert panel.\nWeek of March 19, 2012 - Tribal Consultation with New Mexico\u2019s Tribal leaders to\ndiscuss the concept paper and specifically how it relates to the Native American\nPueblos, Tribes and Nations.\nOngoing - Sidonie on talk radio throughout state, Senator Domenici as surrogate,\nand op-ed farmed out to newspapers statewide\n\nInternal Document - Not for Release",
